#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkCollection-add-support-for-range-based-for-loops.md:1
msgid ""
"Range-based for loops for `vtkCollection`; deprecation of "
"`vtkCollectionIterator`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkCollection-add-support-for-range-based-for-loops.md:3
msgid ""
"`vtkCollection` now supports C++11 range-based for loops, leveraging modern "
"C++ syntax."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkCollection-add-support-for-range-based-for-loops.md:5
msgid ""
"This, along with `vtk::Range`, should be preferred over using "
"`vtkCollectionIterator` and `vtkCollectionSimpleIterator` and they are now "
"deprecated."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkCollection-add-support-for-range-based-for-loops.md:7
msgid "Here's a typical example of the old way:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkCollection-add-support-for-range-based-for-loops.md:9
msgid ""
"vtkCollectionIterator* iter = this->AnimationCuesIterator;\n"
"for (iter->InitTraversal(); !iter->IsDoneWithTraversal(); iter-"
">GoToNextItem())\n"
"{\n"
"  vtkAnimationCue* cue = vtkAnimationCue::SafeDownCast(iter-"
">GetCurrentObject());\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkCollection-add-support-for-range-based-for-loops.md:16
msgid "transformed:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkCollection-add-support-for-range-based-for-loops.md:18
msgid ""
"for (vtkObject* obj : *(this->AnimationCues))\n"
"{\n"
"  vtkAnimationCue* cue = vtkAnimationCue::SafeDownCast(obj);\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkCollection-add-support-for-range-based-for-loops.md:24
msgid ""
"Note that since `vtkCollection` uses `vtkObject` (as opposed to being "
"templated), the range-based for loops also use `vtkObject` and may require "
"casting (as in both the old *and* new ways above)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../release_details/9.7/vtkCollection-add-support-for-range-based-for-loops.md:26
msgid ""
"All of VTK's own uses have been updated. The only slight backwards "
"incompatible change is that the `protected` member `vtkCollectionIterator* "
"AnimationCuesIterator` in `vtkAnimationScene` has been removed. This may "
"cause compatibility issues for anyone subclassing this class."
msgstr ""
